<title>DENMARK: Maersk Air cabin staff call off strike.</title>
<headline>Maersk Air cabin staff call off strike.</headline>
<dateline>COPENHAGEN 1997-03-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Denmark's Maersk Air DSSCb.CO said on Tuesday it reached a new three-year working conditions and pay accord with cabin staff averting a looming strike.</p>
<p>On February 26, Denmark's state arbitration postponed a Maersk Air cabin staff strike by two weeks until March 17 to allow the parties to continue negotiations.</p>
<p>Maersk Air, with 260 cabin staff and owned by Danish shipping and oil group A.P.Moeller, operates flights within Denmark and the Nordic region as well as between Copenhagen and London and Billund, west Denmark, and Frankfurt. --Chris Follett, Copenhagen newsroom +45-33969652</p>
